---
import StudioLayout from '../layouts/StudioLayout.astro';
import { contactEmail } from '../content/site';
---
<StudioLayout title="Terms & Conditions — Sites by Leon" description="Terms for the Sites By Leon website and services." tone="legal">
  <header class="legal-heading"><p class="legal-kicker">Legal</p><h1>Terms &amp; conditions</h1><p class="legal-description">Website and service terms for Sites by Leon.</p><p class="legal-updated">Last updated July 27, 2026</p></header>
  <div class="legal-layout">
    <details class="legal-index" open><summary>On this page</summary><nav class="legal-contents" aria-label="On this page">
      <a href="#about-these-terms">About these terms</a>
      <a href="#website-information-and-examples">Website information and examples</a>
      <a href="#plans-and-project-scope">Plans and project scope</a>
      <a href="#subscriptions-and-cancellation">Subscriptions and cancellation</a>
      <a href="#customer-responsibilities">Customer responsibilities</a>
      <a href="#payments-for-a-customer-s-clients">Payments for a customer's clients</a>
      <a href="#availability-and-changes">Availability and changes</a>
      <a href="#suspension-and-termination">Suspension and termination</a>
      <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
    </nav></details>
    <article class="legal-body">
      <section id="about-these-terms">
        <h2>About these terms</h2>
        <p>These terms apply to the Sites By Leon public website and paid website, hosting, and support services. A written proposal, order, or other agreement may add to these terms; if it conflicts with these terms, the more specific written agreement controls.</p>
      </section>
      <section id="website-information-and-examples">
        <h2>Website information and examples</h2>
        <p>This site describes services offered by Sites By Leon. Website examples marked "Concept Project" are demonstrations and are not commissioned client work. Service descriptions may be updated as the product changes.</p>
      </section>
      <section id="plans-and-project-scope">
        <h2>Plans and project scope</h2>
        <p>The public prices are monthly hosting plans. The selected plan, website pages, content, launch timing, support, and included updates are shown at checkout or confirmed in writing before billing begins. Requests outside the agreed scope may require a separate price or schedule.</p>
      </section>
      <section id="subscriptions-and-cancellation">
        <h2>Subscriptions and cancellation</h2>
        <p>Subscriptions are processed by Stripe and renew according to the billing interval shown at checkout until canceled. Current billing status and cancellation options are available through the customer billing portal. Access may be limited or paused when a subscription is unpaid, canceled, or past due. Any refund terms shown at checkout or agreed in writing apply.</p>
      </section>
      <section id="customer-responsibilities">
        <h2>Customer responsibilities</h2>
        <p>Customers must provide accurate account information, protect access to their accounts, and use the service lawfully. Customers must have the rights and permissions needed for all text, images, trademarks, client information, and other material they provide, upload, or publish.</p>
      </section>
      <section id="payments-for-a-customer-s-clients">
        <h2>Payments for a customer's clients</h2>
        <p>Customer invoice and payment tools require a separate connected Stripe account and successful setup. The customer is responsible for its prices, services, client agreements, taxes, refunds, disputes, and compliance obligations. Sites By Leon is not a party to transactions between a customer and that customer's clients.</p>
      </section>
      <section id="availability-and-changes">
        <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
        <p>Sites By Leon works to keep websites and account tools available and secure, but uninterrupted or error-free service cannot be guaranteed. Maintenance, security work, provider outages, and events outside reasonable control may affect availability. Customers should keep their own copies of important original content.</p>
      </section>
      <section id="suspension-and-termination">
        <h2>Suspension and termination</h2>
        <p>Access may be limited or terminated for nonpayment, unlawful or abusive use, security risk, infringement, or a material violation of these terms. When practical, Sites By Leon will provide notice and an opportunity to correct the issue.</p>
      </section>
      <section id="contact">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.</p>
      </section>
      <a class="studio-text-link" href="/">Return home ↗</a>
    </article>
  </div>
</StudioLayout>
